A||||9||bonnovy||no power to trunk release
Z||000000||bonnovy||04-12-99||07:01 PM||||One fine day I packed my golf clubs,(ya they fit with a pull cart) in the trunk. When I got to the course I hit the trunk release and it clicked a few times and then nothing but the relay noise under the dash. Turned out the bag strap was jammed in the latch. I checked all the fuses I can find. Manual is of no help. Where is this thing fused? (jumping 12v to unit actuates the latch release also) ANYONE?
Z||000001||overlord||04-12-99||08:05 PM||||u said u can hear the click? then the swtich is still working probably...not electrialc but probably mechanical...just check to see that the clubs didnt damage the lock doohickee...thats my guess..
Z||000002||PaUL||04-12-99||08:13 PM||||Hey I got the answer, since the fiero's decklid is plastic, the solenoid for the release MUST ground through the bottom latch. If this ground connection is blocked by something non conductive, the release wont ground and wont work
Z||000003||bonnovy||04-12-99||08:33 PM||||I have the trunk open now (key wouldn't work as it was corroded from previous owner) I had to punch out the lock. Still no power to  solenoid. Are there any fusible links in this line? As stated previous, if I jumper 12v to the solenoid it works, just not from the dash switch. ps thanks for the replys so fast.
Z||000004||PaUL||04-12-99||08:36 PM||||As I was saying, the release wont work if the trunk is open, it only grounds to the lower latch, when its closed. 
Z||000005||PaUL||04-12-99||08:40 PM||||wait a minute, now your saying it doesnt work at all? If so check the 4 wire connector for the release/decklid open warning light next to the battery.<p>If thats ok, then theres a relay under the dash that disables the release when the car is moving, this prevents accicental opening when driving. Check that next.
Z||000006||FieroMike||04-13-99||08:06 AM||||Here is what I would suggest. It sounds like the switch is bad even though you can hear it click.  You can plug the wiring harness on the back of the trunk lid release to the defogger button to see if the switch is bad.  Amazingly enough the defogger will open the trunk but will cause weird problems elsewhere so just try it to see if the switch is bad.  The relay in the trunk has a grounding wire running to it so it will still click with the deck lid open. (At least my two do).  If there is a relay under the dash to disable it that could also be the problem, but mine pops open while I'm moving. (Unfortunately) :-) Good Luck
Z||000007||theogre||04-21-99||09:52 PM||||there is a third part of the power trunk latch option........<p>there is a relay under the dash. it should be located directly below the switch.<p>I just installed this option today. took about an hour. would have been a few minutes less if I got the relay first trip.
Z||000008||theogre||04-22-99||01:21 PM||||the circuit is also park interlocked on auto trany cars. if the park switch is messed up then it won't open either.
Z||000009||theogre||04-22-99||02:51 PM||||btw.... if you need to replace the relay, you can use the same one that the horn uses if the "right" one isn't available at the parts store. the horn relay is just a it heavier design internally, electrically & physically it's the same.
